<title>FINLAND: Baltic Ice - Northern ice thickens, south ice-free.</title>
<headline>Baltic Ice - Northern ice thickens, south ice-free.</headline>
<dateline>HELSINKI 1996-12-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Ice levels remained well below average as ice thickened and its edge at the far northern end of the Gulf of Bothnia moved south to 65 degrees north, the Finnish Institute of Marine Research said on Monday.</p>
<p>Fast ice off the Finnish ports of Kemi and Oulu varied in thickness betwen five and 30 centimetres and off the port of Lulea in Sweden it was between 10 and 20 centimetres thick.</p>
<p>Ports further south were still clear, with water temperatures ranging from one to four degrees Celsius in the Gulf of Bothnia and from one to six degrees in the Gulf of Finland, the institute said.</p>
